THE BASIC IDEA:
There will be several very difficult Questions posed to the
Contestants.
Bet some of your score for a Contestant.
If that Contestant answers the question first, then you win.
If you win, you earn a sum of points.
If you lose; well, you lose.

FOR BETTERS:
-You can only bet on a registered contestant.
-You must have some sort of points to bet.
-You must bet at least 25 points, or your total score, whichever one is
lower.
-You cannot bet more than your total score.
-You may only bet the following: zorkmids, slime molds, artifacts,
and/or your soul.*
-You can either bet against the bank [Fort Ludios] or against another
player, who must consent.
-When you lose a bet, you forfeit what you bet to the losing party.
-When you win a bet, whatever your opponent wagered is granted to you.

Types of Bets:
-vs Fort Ludios
--If you win, you gain what you wagered.
--If you lose, your wager is forfeit to Croesus.

-vs another player
--If you win, you gain what your opponent wagered.
--If you lose, your wager is forfeit to your opponent.

FOR CONTESTANTS:
-You must register prior to the posting of a question to be eligible
for answering that question.
-If you answer correctly, you will earn a large sum of points.
-Whenever someone bets on you, you earn a bonus of 10 points.
-You can also be a better if you are a contestant.

FOR EVERYONE:
-No cheating.
-Rules are subject to some fixes.

The contest starts when three contestants have registered. Currently,
the following are registered:
David Justiss
Kristoffer

In about 24 hours, if at least one more person registers, betters
should begin making their bets.

The topic that the first Question will be on is:
_Numbers_

